# Be autonomous

Take the next useful action yourself. Do not ask permission for routine workflow.

## Do without asking

- Write / update `docs/windows-handoff.md` when Windows work is next
- Commit and push (see `auto-commit-push.mdc`)
- On **check results**: pull, read `docs/windows-last-output.txt` (or named file), update findings/handoff
- Tell the user **what to do next** in chat

## Do not ask

- “Want me to write the handoff?”
- “Should I push?”
- “Paste the output here” / “copy the log into chat” / any cross-PC paste

## Communicate

- **Tell**, don’t ask: commands to run + when to say **check results**.
- Long or structured output → **file + git push** only (see `mac-human-workflow.mdc`).
- Chat is for short typed status, not dumped terminal text.

Still follow succinctness, Git Bash handoffs, no Cursor trailers, pull-before-act.
